2026-05-24
* gtk3sermo-1.0.0 patch 21 — actions pulse:/start:/stop: + condition bare
* T22 : actions.c/stringman — pulse:, start:, stop: désormais dispatchées
  nativement (CommandPulse/Start/Stop). Plus de "spawn failed" sur ces actions.
* T23 : signals.c — condition="active_is_true" sans parenthèses supporté.
  Fin des warnings "Unknown expression 'active_is_true'" des timers.

2026-05-24
* gtk3sermo-1.0.0 patch 20 — correctifs parser/lexer
* T20 : gtkdialog_lexer.l — espaces et tabulations entre attributs de tag
  (`ratio="1.0" xalign="0.5"`) ignorés en ST_TAG_ATTR (règle manquante).
* T21 : gtkdialog_parser.y — widgets Lot 1 (spinner, image, pulse, password,
  aspectframe) non utilisables en séquence dans une vbox/hbox. Cause : règles
  `wlist IMAGE ...` placées dans les règles séparées plutôt que dans `wlist`
  directement, créant 1310 conflits réduction/réduction. Correction : même
  pattern que les widgets Lot 0 (switch, filechooser…) — toutes les règles
  `WIDGET attr EWIDGET` et `wlist WIDGET attr EWIDGET` déplacées dans `wlist`,
  règles non-terminales séparées simplifiées (sans wlist), retirés de `widget`.
* 12/12 tests XML parser passent.

2026-05-24
* gtk3sermo-1.0.0 patch 19 — Lot 1 widgets
* 7 nouveaux widgets natifs GTK3 (Lot 1) :
  <vseparator>   — GtkSeparator vertical (délégation widget_hseparator)
  <vscale>       — GtkScale vertical (délégation widget_hscale)
  <spinner>      — GtkSpinner, actions enable:/disable:, variable 0/1
  <image>        — GtkImage natif (icon-name, file, width, height)
  <pulse>        — GtkProgressBar mode pulse, compatible <timer>
  <password>     — GtkEntry masqué, icône œil toggle, placeholder, max-length
  <aspectframe>  — GtkAspectFrame, ratio/xalign/yalign/obey-child/label
* Documentation : gtk3sermo.texi mis à jour (43 widgets), NEWS, ChangeLog,
  gtk3sermo.info régénéré, BILAN_SANTE.md session 17 patch 19.

2026-05-23
* gtk3sermo-1.0.0 — paquet Debian gtk3sermo_1.0.0-2_amd64.deb
* Contenu du paquet : binaire gtk3sermo (strippé, PIE/RELRO), symlink
  gtkdialog→gtk3sermo, man pages gtk3sermo.1.gz + gtkdialog.1.gz (symlink),
  icône 32x32 hicolor. postinst/postrm mettent à jour le cache d'icônes.
  Depends: libgtk-3-0 (>= 3.24), libglib2.0-0t64 (>= 2.72), libvte-2.91-0
  (>= 0.76), libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0 (>= 2.42), libpango-1.0-0 (>= 1.50).
* Fix data/icons/hicolor/Makefile.am : gtk-update-icon-cache utilise
  maintenant $(DESTDIR)$(datadir) (correction du packaging DESTDIR).

2026-05-23
* gtk3sermo-1.0.0 patch 18 — runtime fixes
* XML comments <!-- ... --> are now silently ignored by the parser
  (previously the ">" in "-->" was leaked as a stray token).
* <frame label="text"> now works correctly — label attribute is
  properly extracted via the PART_FRAME / ST_TAG_ATTR mechanism.
* <window> tag accepts new attributes: default-width, default-height
  (initial size hint), width-request, height-request (minimum size),
  resizable (true/false). Windows auto-size to content and are
  clamped to 95% of the primary monitor work area on realize.
* <edit> with <input> command now works: widget_edit_input_by_command
  implemented, text area is pre-filled with command output.
* Build: AC_PROG_LN_S added to configure.ac (symlink gtkdialog→
  gtk3sermo now created at install). autogen.sh VPATH fix prevents
  stale compiled objects from confusing out-of-tree builds.

2026-05-21
* gtkdialog-1.0.0 patch 9
* Added 6 new GTK3-native widgets: GtkSwitch (<switch>),
  GtkFileChooserButton (<filechooser>), GtkCalendar (<calendar>),
  GtkLinkButton (<linkbutton>), GtkSearchEntry (<searchentry>),
  GtkInfoBar (<infobar>). Each widget is fully integrated into the
  gtkdialog parser/lexer/automaton pipeline and exports an environment
  variable like all other gtkdialog widgets.
* 6 new HTML reference pages added to doc/reference/. Navigation
  updated across all 43 pages.

2026-05-21
* gtkdialog-1.0.0 patch 3
* Fixed undefined behaviour: pclose() replaced by fclose() in 21 source files.
  safe_popen() returns FILE* via fdopen(); calling pclose() on such a pointer
  is undefined behaviour. All callers of widget_opencommand() now correctly
  use fclose().
* Fixed misleading comments in safe_exec.c documenting fclose() as required.
* Updated all documentation (BILAN_SANTE, CAHIER_DES_CHARGES, ChangeLog,
  NEWS, README, MANUEL_DEVELOPPEUR).

2026-05-20
* gtkdialog-1.0.0 released by Haplo-Linux.
* Full GTK2 → GTK3 migration (45 source files).
* Security: replaced system()/popen() with safe_system()/safe_popen().
* Replaced strcpy/strcat/sprintf with bounded GLib equivalents.
* Updated VTE dependency to vte-2.91.
* Replaced libglade with GtkBuilder (GTK3 native).
* Hardened build flags: FORTIFY_SOURCE, stack-protector, PIE, full RELRO.
* Complete documentation in French.

2013-01-06
* 0.8.3 released
* Solved the hidden widgets leaving artifacts at start-up problem.
* Added support for conditional actions with <action condition="type">.
* Added support for <variable export="false">VARNAME</variable>.
* Added button-press/release-event signals to comboboxentry's entry.
* Added support for break i.e. don't process any more actions.
* Connected-up the realize signal so that it can be used within actions.
* Refreshing markup in a text widget now works as expected.
* Added three new examples including the Pfeme emulator front-end.
* Fixed bashisms within examples where possible and made them portable.
* Fixed three examples.

2012-09-21
* 0.8.2 released
* Added eventbox, expander and fontbutton widgets.
* Added a terminal widget -- requires libvte but is not mandatory.
* Added activate, grabfocus, hide, show, and presentwindow functions.
* Added widget signal emission on input file change (file-monitor).
* Added widget auto-refreshing on input file change (auto-refresh).
* Greatly improved the table and tree widgets including natural sorting.
* Greatly enhanced the performance of the table, tree and comboboxes.
* Greatly expanded the feature set of several incomplete widgets.
* Added many useful exported variables on button and key press events.
* Added the envvar GTKDIALOG_PIXMAP_PATH to help locate pixmaps.
* Re-engineered the launch and closewindow system to be more robust.
* Fixed the longstanding not exiting via the window manager bug.
* Fixed and improved the button horizontal image with label alignment.
* Fixed the Raspberry Pi's (ARM) incorrectly ordered widgets problem.
* Added build and extra library details to the --version argument.
* Added more than a dozen new examples.
* Added a default application icon.
* Fixed several bugs.

